# Original writer fixture: split, converge, split again, and finish.
:: alarm default
> speaker=ivo @alarm_line
  The lower gate is stuck open, and the market is still full of people.
? @take_rooftops
  I'll ring the roof bell. You clear the stairs.
  -> rooftops
? @take_market
  Come with me. We'll clear the stalls together.
  -> market

:: rooftops
> speaker=lea @rooftops_line
  From up here I can see the water crossing the square.
> speaker=ivo @bell_line
  They heard you. The stairs are moving.
-> gatehouse

:: market
> speaker=lea @market_line
  Leave the carts! The upper street is still dry.
> speaker=ivo @market_reply
  That's the last stallholder. She wouldn't leave without her cat.
-> gatehouse

:: gatehouse
> speaker=ivo @gatehouse_line
  Everyone's out. Now we either cut the gate loose or turn the water through the workshops.
? @cut_chain
  Cut the chain. We'll rebuild the gate.
  -> broken_gate
? @open_sluice
  Open the side sluice. Save the foundations.
  -> flooded_workshops

:: broken_gate
> speaker=lea @chain_line
  Stand back. When it falls, nothing holds it.
> speaker=ivo @gate_falls
  There it goes. A year's repairs in one splash.
-> high_ground

:: flooded_workshops
> speaker=lea @sluice_line
  Help me with the wheel. Don't look at the windows.
> speaker=ivo @workshop_loss
  My sister works down there. I'll tell her myself.
-> high_ground

:: high_ground
> speaker=ivo @high_ground_line
  Everyone's accounted for. They're waiting to hear what happened.
? @tell_truth
  Then we tell them together.
  -> together
? @take_blame
  I'll speak. It was my decision.
  -> alone

:: together
> speaker=lea @together_line
  Give us a moment, everyone. We owe you the whole story.
-> END

:: alone
> speaker=lea @alone_line
  I made a choice down there. You deserve to know why.
-> END
